## <gno-icon name="terminal" /> From your terminal

gnodev funds the gnokey keys it finds at startup, so add yours first. Then call your realm:

```sh
gnokey add alice

gnokey maketx call \
  -pkgpath "{{.Realm}}" \
  -func "<Func>" \
  -gas-fee 10000ugnot -gas-wanted 10000000 \
  -chainid {{.ChainID}} -remote {{.RPC}} \
  alice
```

A realm's Actions page writes a ready-to-run command for each function.

Need a package only mainnet has? Start gnodev with its code; its state starts empty:

```sh
gnodev -remote gno.land=https://rpc.gno.land:443 .
```

