## <gno-icon name="rocket" /> Ship it to the testnet

When it works here, deploy its folder to onyx under your address. A package of yours that it imports goes first, and the import then points at your address. Get test GNOT first: keys are not funded there. Onyx enables a deploy a few seconds after it lands.

```sh
gnokey maketx addpkg \
  -pkgpath "gno.land/r/<your-g1-addr>/{{.RealmName}}" \
  -pkgdir "{{.RealmDir}}" \
  -gas-fee 40000ugnot -gas-wanted 20000000 \
  -chainid onyx-1 -remote https://rpc.onyx.testnets.gno.land:443 \
  alice
```

<gno-button href="https://faucet.gno.land" label="Open the faucet" /> <gno-button href="https://docs.gno.land/builders/getting-started#deploy-to-a-shared-network" label="Deploy guide" variant="outline" />

